Let $V$ be a simple unitary strongly rational vertex operator algebra, and let $W$ be a grading-restricted unitary $V$-module. Every vertex operator on $W$ satisfies polynomial energy bounds. More precisely, if $a\in V_d$ is quasi-primary, $d\geq2$, and $(-1)^d\Theta a=a$, then there are constants $C_a>0$ and $p_a\in\mathbb Z_{\geq0}$ such that $$\label{eq:optimal-vertex-bound}
 \|a[m]\xi\|
 \leq C_a(1+|m|)^{p_a}
       \|(1+L_0)^{d-1}\xi\|,
 \qquad m\in\mathbb Z,\quad \xi\in W.$$ Weight-one fields and the Virasoro field satisfy energy bounds of at most linear order. The constants may depend on $V$, $W$, and $a$.

For a monomial $b$ in <a href="#eq:energy-monomial" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:energy-monomial">[eq:energy-monomial]</a> of weight $w\geq2$, there are constants $C_b,c_b$ such that $$\label{eq:sharp-normal-product}
 \|b[0]P_N\|
 \leq C_b N^{w-1}X_{N+c_b}^{D_b}\qquad(N\geq1).$$ At weights zero and one the corresponding bounds are a constant and $C_bN^{1/2}X_N$, respectively.

Let $\widehat A=\underline A^\dagger\underline A$ be a fixed localized double, and let $S_0$ be a closed round disc strictly inside it. There is a constant $C_{\widehat A,S_0}$ such that, for every Möbius embedding $p:\mathbb D\to\mathring S_0$ and $v\in V$, $$\label{eq:fixed-disc-bound}
 \|\widehat A_N[p_*v(0)]\|
     \leq C_{\widehat A,S_0}\|v\|$$ in every already integrated unitary module $N$. Here $\mathbb D$ is the closed unit disc, and embeddings are smooth up to their boundaries.

Let $N$ be an already integrated unitary $V$-module. Set $$a=1-10^{-4},\qquad
 \gamma_t(\zeta)=\frac{\zeta+t}{1+t\zeta},\qquad
 r=\gamma_t(a),\qquad s=\gamma_t(1/2),\qquad 0\leq t<1.$$ With $\delta=r^{-1}-r$ and $q=2\delta$, there is a constant $C_N$, independent of $t$ and $v$, such that $$\label{eq:uniform-round}
 \|A_{1/s,s,N}[(q^{L_0}v)(r)]\|\leq C_N\|v\|,
 \qquad v\in V.$$ Moreover, $$\label{eq:round-comparable}
 5000\leq\frac{1-s}{1-r}\leq6667.$$

Let $M,N$ be unitary modules, with $N$ already integrated. For homogeneous $a,a'\in M$ of weights $d,d'$, set $$u_z=\mathcal Y_M^-(\theta_{\bar z}a',\bar z^{-1}-z)a,
 \qquad \delta=|z|^{-1}-|z|,\qquad q=2\delta.$$ As $|z|$ tends to one on a fixed branch, $$\label{eq:annulus-hilbert-state}
 q^{-L_0}u_z\in\mathcal H_V,
 \qquad \|q^{-L_0}u_z\|\leq C_{a,a'}\delta^{-d-d'}.$$ For a fixed dent with $z$ in its inner collar, $\widehat A_N[u_z(z)]$ is well defined by norm limits of energy truncations, belongs to $\pi_I^N(A_V(I))$, and has norm at most $C\delta^{-d-d'}$. On $\underline A_N^{-1}N$ in both variables it obeys $$\label{eq:transport-cutoff}
 \langle\widehat A_N[u_z(z)]\xi,\eta\rangle
 =\mathfrak t_z^{M,N}
   (a\otimes\underline A_N\xi,
    a'\otimes\underline A_N\eta).$$ For the round annuli of Proposition <a href="#prop:round-annulus" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="prop:round-annulus">8</a>, the same bound holds with the cutoffs $s^{L_0}$ in both entries and $z=r$.

Let $V$ be a simple unitary strongly rational VOA. Its conformal net $A_V$ is completely rational. The CWX functor constructed in Theorem <a href="#thm:cwx-embedding" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="thm:cwx-embedding">19</a> is essentially surjective onto the additive category of finite-index locally normal DHR representations of $A_V$. Consequently it is a braided unitary tensor equivalence $$F^V_{\mathrm{CWX}}:
  \operatorname{Rep}^{u}(V)\xrightarrow{\ \simeq\ }
  \operatorname{Rep}^{f}(A_V).$$
